{"captions": [{"t": 0.0, "d": 2.49, "text": "What if moving Cook Inlet power"}, {"t": 2.52, "d": 2.8, "text": "means moving the computer instead?"}, {"t": 6.42, "d": 3.39, "text": "DeepGreen proposes sixty-six compute"}, {"t": 9.84, "d": 1.62, "text": "hives near Nikiski."}, {"t": 12.3, "d": 4.981, "text": "Around them, three hundred thirty to three hundred fifty marine"}, {"t": 17.281, "d": 1.739, "text": "hydrokinetic turbines."}, {"t": 19.88, "d": 2.27, "text": "The turbines would power them directly"}, {"t": 22.18, "d": 2.96, "text": "while seawater provides passive cooling."}, {"t": 25.68, "d": 0.53, "text": "Clever."}, {"t": 26.24, "d": 3.17, "text": "Put the primary load beside its"}, {"t": 29.44, "d": 1.08, "text": "proposed power source."}, {"t": 31.6, "d": 2.53, "text": "A 3.5 mile cable"}, {"t": 34.16, "d": 2.56, "text": "would carry power and fiber ashore."}, {"t": 38.06, "d": 3.18, "text": "The notice estimates 100 MW."}, {"t": 42.1, "d": 0.7, "text": "Where would it go?"}, {"t": 44.08, "d": 2.48, "text": "The data center would be the primary use."}, {"t": 47.62, "d": 5.52, "text": "Only spare power could reach the Railbelt. Could, not will."}, {"t": 54.12, "d": 3.28, "text": "Now put that diagram on a test bench."}, {"t": 58.3, "d": 3.52, "text": "The filing names no customer or committed financing."}, {"t": 62.9, "d": 2.6, "text": "No completed proof covers output,"}, {"t": 66.04, "d": 2.48, "text": "cooling, economics, grid connection,"}, {"t": 68.94, "d": 1.12, "text": "or environmental effects."}, {"t": 70.9, "d": 4.14, "text": "That doesn't make it bad. It makes the next step a study."}, {"t": 75.9, "d": 4.01, "text": "On September fourth, FERC opened public comment on the application."}, {"t": 79.94, "d": 4.14, "text": "If issued, the permit gives study priority."}, {"t": 85.02, "d": 1.47, "text": "It wouldn't authorize construction"}, {"t": 86.52, "d": 3.12, "text": "or prove that one turbine works there."}, {"t": 90.28, "d": 4.025, "text": "Com